abstract:
The two boosters that took XGBoost's crown for specific problems. LightGBM grows trees leaf-wise and throws away boring rows and useless feature pairs, buying a large speed-up on wide data. CatBoost solves the categorical-variable problem properly with ordered target statistics and removes the prediction shift that leaks labels into training. We measure both against XGBoost and show exactly where each wins.}
